WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.068
Go outside.

2
00:00:01.228 --> 00:00:04.386
A park, a garden or a path is full of art ideas.

3
00:00:04.546 --> 00:00:08.819
Leaves, feathers, pebbles and shells all have shapes, colours and textures.

4
00:00:08.979 --> 00:00:14.737
Collect only what has already fallen, never put anything in your mouth, and wash your hands afterwards.

5
00:00:15.437 --> 00:00:16.644
Touch and sort.

6
00:00:16.804 --> 00:00:18.105
Touch your treasures.

7
00:00:18.265 --> 00:00:19.472
Bark is rough.

8
00:00:19.632 --> 00:00:20.979
A pebble is smooth.

9
00:00:21.139 --> 00:00:22.579
A feather is soft.

10
00:00:22.739 --> 00:00:26.315
Sorting them by how they feel is one way of remembering the walk.

11
00:00:27.015 --> 00:00:28.268
Draw from life.

12
00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:32.051
Drawing from life means looking at a real thing while you draw it.

13
00:00:32.211 --> 00:00:33.232
Look first.

14
00:00:33.392 --> 00:00:35.993
A leaf has a straight vein and a jagged edge.

15
00:00:36.153 --> 00:00:37.500
A pebble is round.

16
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.236
At home, put a real leaf in front of you and draw what is really there.

17
00:00:41.936 --> 00:00:43.004
Land art.

18
00:00:43.164 --> 00:00:46.089
Some artists make art outside, from what they find.

19
00:00:46.249 --> 00:00:49.407
They lay leaves in a circle, or stones in a line.

20
00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:51.053
It is called land art.

21
00:00:51.213 --> 00:00:54.418
The wind and rain may take it away, so they take a photo.
